# `prettier --check .` and with it the pre-commit hook — on a file no human
# wrote and nothing in the repo reads.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The stand's disposable home. The e2e container runs as root, so this is
# root-owned after a local run and a walker that enters it fails outright
# rather than merely wasting time.
.e2e/

# Negative lint fixtures (Rule 9, ADR-0024). Deliberately broken code — they
# are linted explicitly by src/eslint-fixture-gate.test.ts, excluded from the
# normal lint/typecheck runs, and must not be reformatted by prettier either.
eslint-fixtures/

# Agent-tooling scratch, the same class as .agents/ and .claude/ above: the
# SDD brief/report workspace (written per worktree by the beads-superpowers
# plugin, self-ignored by a generated .gitignore), the briefs a coordinator
# hands a herdr worker, and repowise's index. All exist only on a machine
# running those tools, so CI never sees them — but `prettier --check .` walks
# the filesystem rather than the index, so they failed the ci-frontend job
# locally while the same job was green on the runner, on files no human wrote
# and nothing in the repo reads.
#
# These are named one directory at a time rather than as `.internal/` because
# the rest of that tree is TRACKED PROSE — briefs, specs, plans, handoffs —
# which prettier formats and should go on formatting. So the list grows by one
# line each time a tool invents a new scratch directory, and `.internal/handoff/`
# is the second (nocx-x4i5z).
.internal/sdd/
.internal/handoff/
.repowise/

# Память репозитория для cass-memory. Файл генерируется
# scripts/bd-memories-to-cass.py из .internal/memories-export.jsonl, и
# переформатировать его — значит поставить prettier против генератора: следующий
# прогон вернёт свою раскладку, и гейт снова покраснеет. То же основание, что у
# .beads/ выше: это вывод инструмента, а не текст, который кто-то писал руками.
.cass/playbook.yaml
